Each building is modeled as a graph $G=(V,E)$, where $V=\{1, \dots, N\}$ and $E \subseteq V \times V$ are the nodes and edges (Figure \ref{fig:example_graph}). Nodes correspond to rooms, with hallways discretized into multiple nodes based on room adjacency. Edges represent the connections between rooms. To allow evacuees to stay in place, we include self-loops $(i,i) \in E$.

