In practice, latency for GPEvac is exceptionally low. For the Acyclic and Cyclic schools (55 and 70 nodes), GPEvac has a median inference time of just $14.73$ ms (95th percentile: $15.46$ ms), comfortably outpacing standard surveillance camera frame rates. Even for graphs exceeding 1,000 nodes, far larger than typical building layouts, inference executes in a fraction of a second. This means that GPEvac can deliver continuous, real-time routing updates in deployment without relying on high-end GPU hardware.

